WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.297
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.470
SEAN YOU: Our company is
a leading mobility service

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.000
provider here in South Korea.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.150
And our user base is more
than 30 million users,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.570
which means most people in
South Korea use our services.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.780
Our DevOps philosophy is to
detect and recover the failure

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.160
as fast as we can.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.010
Since our ride-hailing service
and [INAUDIBLE] services

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.310
are so critical to our users,
we put relentless effort

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.810
to achieve zero downtime.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.670
Therefore, our
DevOps team mainly

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.759
focuses on improving the
detectability of system

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.580
failures and designing
[INAUDIBLE] systems that

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.210
can recover automatically.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.830
So in this project, we wanted
to re-architecture our systems

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.800
so that we can operate
our microservices,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.190
both in our [INAUDIBLE] Cloud
and Google Cloud Platform

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.510
simultaneously.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.000
The first objective was to
build an environment that

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.250
can respond to the heavy
[INAUDIBLE] traffic.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.110
In case of the sudden
traffic increases,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.680
we were able to acquire
additional resources in Google

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.990
Cloud Platform very
smoothly instead

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.160
of acquiring on-prem resources.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.960
So I think the future growth is
order of kind of two or three

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.340
times in terms of traffic
and then the kind of service

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.560
we need to provide in
terms of your growth.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.880
So that would be
huge if you think

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.030
about the amount of
traffic we handle today.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.810
Additional resources
were required.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.800
So we rebalanced the traffic
so that a large amount

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.770
of on-prem traffic could be
processed in Google Cloud

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.610
Platform.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:33.060
The past increase, according
to the HPA settings in the GKE,

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.090
based on the number of
cores in GCP resources--

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.850
it increased about four
times compared to the usual.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:43.050
And it increased from the
previously set quota, 20%,

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.300
to about 80%.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.940
Our project team's capability
have grown together

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.700
with Google teams enduring
support, especially customer,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.490
engineer, and technical
account managers.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.550
There is bi-weekly regular
meeting with our DevOps team,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.980
GCP team, and GCP's partner.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.020
GCP customer success
manager has taken

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.070
care of all the required GCP
learning classes we needed.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.590
Also, it becomes a unique
differentiated point

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.190
to talk about a long-term
perspective roadmap

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.430
and further collaboration
point between GCP and us.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.160
Under the strong support
from the Google Cloud team,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.980
we were able to expedite
a work in progress

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.950
to get into stable
first migration to GCP.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.020
It was a very
pleasant experience

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.790
to work together as a team.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.640
And I expect more collaboration
in this year as well.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.010
Project was very challenging
for our DevOps team,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.650
since we only have
used on-prem cloud.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.660
Learning new
technologies as well as

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.300
operating seamlessly between
two different infrastructures

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.400
was very difficult.
And migrating

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.340
the new architecture-- migrating
to the new architecture

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.773
with zero service downtime
was very challenging as well.

00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:50.190
However, thanks to the support
from the Google Cloud Korea

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.370
team, we were able to
migrate the service smoothly.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.370
And we were very happy with
the successful migration.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.720
[MUSIC PLAYING]

